<title>UK: Sweden sets 17.5 bln yen dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>Sweden sets 17.5 bln yen dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual-currency bond was announced by lead manager Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWEDEN</p>
<p> AMT    17.5 BLN YEN  COUPON   * 7.10	MATURITY    30.OCT.97</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL-CURRENCY ISS PRICE  100	 PAY DATE    30.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.60	REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> NOTES    * REDEMPTION IN NEW ZEALAND DOLLARS</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    NONE	DENOMS (K) 500</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 500	 SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
